# Approved runtime hash of Enshrouded's live config,
# data/game/server/enshrouded_server.json (see manifest.json live_config).
#
# It is a hash of the CONTENT, not the file's bytes: the server rewrites that
# file in its own layout a few seconds after every start, so the watcher parses
# it, blanks the join password, and hashes it with keys sorted and "," / ":" as
# separators. The exact approved content is published next to this file in
# approved-config.json, so anyone can reproduce the value below:
#
#     python3 -c "import json,hashlib; d=json.load(open('approved-config.json')); print(hashlib.sha256(json.dumps(d, sort_keys=True, separators=(',',':'), ensure_ascii=False).encode()).hexdigest())"
#
# Re-run `python3 watcher/watcher.py --approve enshrouded` and commit BOTH files
# whenever a setting legitimately changes - or when a game update adds a new
# setting to the file, which also changes the hash and raises a drift alert
# until it has been looked at and approved.
# The first non-comment line below is read as the hash:
02122d31351f4039b979849c0258b491bb16a2850bff3068dda42c52ada9687a
